Z||000003||Hock||07-16-99||12:23 PM||||Ahhh, tell them some aliens came down from Jupiter and took your poor Fiero to do evil test on it to see what makes it the best car ever made.<br>Or, just unhook the wires going from the ECM to the distributor, this will completly disable the car, and say that there is something majorly wrong with it and you have to send it to a garage to get it fixed.<p>So there you go, if that is too hard for you just fess-up and tell them that they can't drive it because you know that they will abuse it and can't drive all that well in the first place. But either way good luck! 
Z||000004||batboy||07-16-99||05:53 PM||||I prefer the honest approach with parents. Tell them that it's your baby and since they messed it up last time they drove it, you don't want to loan it out anymore. Offer to get them a rental car, if you feel guilty enough or if they put a guilt trip on you. Your dad is probably just trying to pay you back for all the times you did the same things to his cars, back in your youth (haha).
